{"parentUuid":"95ee9bdd-6555-4cea-a618-753736eb15c3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfeAD4D8852aLmtGt1XaU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Context:** Resumed a paused KeystoneOS / claude-skills audit session (AIOS Gate B/C work), then ran the `/mattpocock-skills:handoff` skill to capture state before stopping.\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- The skill-roster checker was validated clean: 16/16 fixtures correct, agreement with the real YAML parser on all 42 skills, live roster failing only the 7 disabled skills, and all 4 fail-closed cases exiting 2.\n- A sleep-induced API error plus a DNS failure (ENOTFOUND) cut off a response mid-run; the user said \"resume\".\n- Claude could not invoke the handoff skill itself — that skill is user-invocation-only, so the user had to type `/mattpocock-skills:handoff`.\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- Three independent items were approved and run: commit/push the checker fix in KeystoneOS, write the Gate B round 2 dispositions, and add Gate B round 2 to the execution log.\n- Handoff doc written to the OS temp dir (not the workspace), linking to plan/log/report paths instead of copying content.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- Some plugin skills are gated to user invocation only; an agent cannot start them. Ask the user to type the slash command.\n- Codex quota exhaustion (reset 10:41 PM) blocks review gates — sequence Codex re-inspection around the reset rather than retrying.\n- Staged-but-uncommitted fixes (C-01 executable bit) are easy to lose across a session break; commit before pausing.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Pending user decisions: (1) the 7 skills off in Claude but live in Codex/Pi — ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review, pp-espn, session-miner — recommend retiring from canonical unless `library-review` or `pp-espn` is used in Codex; (2) Task 8 Pi trial step 1 needs `sudo` — recommend the user runs it.\n- Gate C remaining: commit C-01, fix C-02 (lock race), fix C-03 (usage counts cover Claude only).\n- Codex re-inspection of manifest fix `7459560` after quota reset; then Gate D; then update `docs/STATUS.md`.\n- Commit the BLOCKED Task 8 report at `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t8-pi-trial.md`.\n- Still-open task from earlier: write the project-level skill at `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md` (8-part read-only audit procedure).\n- Handoff file: `/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/handoff-2026-09-13-aios-gate-c.md`\n- Last commits: `7459560` (claude-skills), `08bf6e8` (KeystoneOS)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35545,"cache_read_input_tokens":10906,"output_tokens":984,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35545,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":984,"cache_read_input_tokens":10906,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35545,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35545},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfeAD3xW4wWrFpcM6Ev9Y","type":"assistant","uuid":"79483c0f-7030-4f06-938d-4f4ddf4f8266","timestamp":"2026-10-02T21:58:24.314Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"d9a4f264-3b70-42fb-9429-0768994631a1","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"79483c0f-7030-4f06-938d-4f4ddf4f8266","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__batch","description":"Create a doc, or apply several operations to one doc atomically.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"batch":{"type":"array"},"container":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string"},"id":{"type":"string"},"create":{"type":"object"}},"required":["kind"]},"verbose":{"type":"boolean"},"opId":{"type":"string"}}},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__guide","description":"Docs guides: topic.instructions repeats the server instructions. Read it only if your client dropped them. Also topic.<name>, refusal.<code>. After a doc's birth → [\"topic.index\"].","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"items":{"type":"array","description":"topic.<name> (instructions, index, editing, tabs, comments, charts, chart-definition, diagram, uploads, sharing, skill) or refusal.<code>; several per call is fine."}}},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__update","description":"Edit a tab's contents, rename a doc or tab, or change a stored value.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ref":{"type":"object","properties":{"object":{"type":"string","enum":["project","file","node","utterance","enum"]},"id":{"type":"string"}},"required":["object","id"]},"engine":{"type":"string"},"payload":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object"},{"type":"string"}]},"container":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string"},"id":{"type":"string"},"version":{"type":"string"}},"required":["kind","id"]},"verbose":{"type":"boolean"},"opId":{"type":"string"},"answering":{"type":"string","maxLength":64}},"required":["ref","payload"]},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Firecrawl__firecrawl_scrape","description":"\nScrape one URL and return its content, or execute catalogued Alexandria capabilities. URL mode returns markdown by default, or HTML, links, screenshots, branding data, a targeted answer, or JSON matching a supplied schema, plus page metadata. Firecrawl may serve recently indexed content; set `maxAge: 0` for a live fetch. A successful response does not by itself confirm the page is still current. A named browser profile loads saved session data.\n\n`firecrawl_search` with `sources` unset and `firecrawl_find_tools` can discover providers for the same fields across several pages; a matching Alexandria provider returns typed records in one call.\n\nAlexandria mode: `alexandria` selects catalogued capability execution and is mutually exclusive with `url`. Alexandria execution is billed at the capability's listed price and needs a team with Alexandria enabled.\n","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri"},"formats":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["markdown","html","rawHtml","screenshot","links","summary","changeTracking","branding","json","query","audio"]}},"jsonOptions":{"type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string"},"schema":{"type":"object","propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"additionalProperties":false}},"additionalProperties":false},"queryOptions":{"type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","maxLength":10000},"mode":{"default":"freeform","type":"string","enum":["directQuote","freeform"]}},"required":["prompt"],"additionalProperties":false},"screenshotOptions":{"type":"object","properties":{"fullPage":{"type":"boolean"},"quality":{"type":"number"},"viewport":{"type":"object","properties":{"width":{"type":"number"},"height":{"type":"number"}},"required":["width","height"],"additionalProperties":false}},"additionalProperties":false},"parsers":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["pdf"]}},"pdfOptions":{"type":"object","properties":{"maxPages":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":10000}},"additionalProperties":false},"onlyMainContent":{"type":"boolean"},"redactPII":{"type":"boolean"},"includeTags":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"excludeTags":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"waitFor":{"type":"number"},"mobile":{"type":"boolean"},"skipTlsVerification":{"type":"boolean"},"removeBase64Images":{"type":"boolean"},"location":{"type":"object","properties":{"country":{"type":"string"},"languages":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"additionalProperties":false},"storeInCache":{"type":"boolean"},"zeroDataRetention":{"type":"boolean"},"maxAge":{"type":"number"},"lockdown":{"type":"boolean"},"proxy":{"type":"string","enum":["basic","stealth","enhanced","auto"]},"profile":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"saveChanges":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false},"timeout":{"description":"Execution timeout in milliseconds.","type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},"requestId":{"description":"Idempotency key bound to one Alexandria execution payload. Generated when omitted and returned with the result.","type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9._:-]{1,128}$"},"alexandria":{"description":"Catalogued Alexandria capability invocation, mutually exclusive with url. One {provider, capability, options} object or an array of 1-10, with contracts available through firecrawl_search or firecrawl_find_tools. Each call may include version to pin a published workflow; omitting it uses latest. Only requestId and timeout are supported alongside alexandria. The selected contract marks required inputs and any requiresOneOf groups (at least one member per group); it may include example.request/example.response and response.key (which may differ from records). Where pagination is declared, its fields govern paging with the same filters; catalogue next is separate from provider pagination. Returns per-capability results in data.alexandria with data, records, or an error with a code; individual capabilities can fail even when the outer response succeeds. Requires an API key on a team with Alexandria enabled. Some providers require accepted terms; blocked requests return the applicable requirements.","anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"provider":{"description":"Provider slug, e.g. \"fred\".","type":"string","minLength":1},"capability":{"description":"Capability address as returned by search or discover, e.g. \"series/observations\".","type":"string","minLength":1},"version":{"description":"Optional published workflow version. Omit to use the latest version.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128},"options":{"description":"Capability options as declared by its contract.","type":"object","propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"additionalProperties":{}}},"required":["provider","capability"]},{"minItems":1,"maxItems":10,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"provider":{"description":"Provider slug, e.g. \"fred\".","type":"string","minLength":1},"capability":{"description":"Capability address as returned by search or discover, e.g. \"series/observations\".","type":"string","minLength":1},"version":{"description":"Optional published workflow version. Omit to use the latest version.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128},"options":{"description":"Capability options as declared by its contract.","type":"object","propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"additionalProperties":{}}},"required":["provider","capability"]}}]},"toolDetail":{"description":"URL mode only: domain discovery detail, summary by default; compact returns provider/capability/description, full includes contracts. Ignored with alexandria.","type":"string","enum":["compact","summary","full"]},"domainTools":{"description":"URL mode only: include domain-matched Alexandria tools for the page in tools on the returned document. Ignored with alexandria.","type":"boolean"}},"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"mcp__claude_ai_Firecrawl__firecrawl_search","description":"\nSearch web and specialized indexes, returning ranked results with query-relevant highlights. Each web result is a title, URL, and description. Operators include quoted phrases, `-term`, `site:host`, `inurl:term`, `intitle:term`, and `related:host`; the set is non-exhaustive. `includeDomains` and `excludeDomains` are mutually exclusive hostname filters; categories limit result types to `research`, `pdf`, or `developer`.\n\nFor a programming question, add `categories: [\"developer\"]`. It searches an index of public repositories, GitHub issues, merged pull requests, repository READMEs, and code documentation, and returns the results in `data.web` with `category: \"developer\"`.\n\nAuthenticated search combines web results, semantic tool summaries and domain matches. Use sources: [\"alexandria\"] for semantic tools only. A search with sources: [\"web\"] omits semantic provider discovery; domainTools: true can still return website-matched tools. Web-only results use domainTools: false. Tool matches describe available structured-data capabilities, not executed data. toolDetail: \"compact\" (default) returns only provider, capability and description; \"summary\" adds metadata; \"full\" includes their input and output contracts. firecrawl_scrape with an alexandria body executes a selected capability; firecrawl_find_tools provides catalogue browsing and full contracts.\n\nReturns result groups in `data` and an operation `id`.\n","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"toolDetail":{"description":"Compact by default. Compact returns only provider, capability and description; full includes contracts. Inspect selected compact tools with firecrawl_find_tools providers and capabilities.","type":"string","enum":["compact","summary","full"]},"query":{"description":"Query for web and semantic tool discovery. Operators include quoted phrases, `-term`, `site:host`, `inurl:term`, `intitle:term`, and `related:host`; the set is non-exhaustive. Catalogue browsing is available through firecrawl_find_tools.","type":"string","minLength":1},"objective":{"description":"Optional broader goal for this search, if known. Avoid sensitive information.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":5000},"clientModel":{"description":"Optional model identifier, if known.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128},"domainTools":{"description":"Include domain-matched tools for result URLs. Defaults to true when Alexandria is combined with web, news or images; semantic-only search leaves domain matching off.","type":"boolean"},"highlights":{"description":"Return query-relevant page excerpts for web and news results when available (default). Highlights appear in web `description` and news `snippet`; otherwise, original snippets are returned. Set to false to keep the original search snippets.","type":"boolean"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100},"tbs":{"type":"string"},"filter":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"includeDomains":{"description":"Hostnames to restrict results to. Mutually exclusive with excludeDomains.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":253,"pattern":"^(?:[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?\\.)+[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9]$"}},"excludeDomains":{"description":"Hostnames to leave out of results. Mutually exclusive with includeDomains.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":253,"pattern":"^(?:[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?\\.)+[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9]$"}},"sources":{"description":"Search sources; authenticated sessions default to web + alexandria, keyless sessions to web only. A search with sources: [\"web\"] omits semantic provider discovery; domainTools: true can still return website-matched tools. Web-only results use domainTools: false. Use [\"alexandria\"] alone for provider discovery without web results.","type":"array","items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["web","images","news","alexandria","exchange"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","enum":["web","images","news","alexandria","exchange"]}},"required":["type"],"additionalProperties":false}]}},"categories":{"description":"Limit results to specific source types. `research` restricts ordinary web results to research-affiliated websites and returns page snippets, which is separate from the `firecrawl_research_*` tools that search paper abstracts and full text across biomedical (PubMed, bioRxiv, medRxiv) and arXiv literature; `pdf` searches PDF results; `developer` searches an index built for coding agents over public repositories, GitHub issues, merged pull requests, repository READMEs, and code documentation. `developer` returns hits in `data.web` with `category: \"developer\"`; the other categories also filter `data.web`.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["research","pdf","developer"]}},"enterprise":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["default","anon","zdr"]}}},"required":["query"],"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0bffffcf-be3a-436e-9e73-931dff2f4262","timestamp":"2026-10-02T21:58:24.345Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"d9a4f264-3b70-42fb-9429-0768994631a1","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
